  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Int. R&#xe5;det f&#xf6;r frivilligorganisationer</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Council of Voluntary Agencies (ICVA)2013-2017 - International Council of Voluntary Agencies (ICVA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICVA is a nonprofit global association of over 70 non-governmental    organizations (NGOs)advocating for the promotion of human rights and  the humanitarian perspective in the global debate and humanitarian    response.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ICVA &#xe4;r det st&#xf6;rsta globala humanit&#xe4;ra CSO n&#xe4;tverket med knappt 80 medlemsorganisationer som arbetar f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja det humanit&#xe4;ra perspektivet i den globala debatten och st&#xe4;rka en principiell och effektiv humanit&#xe4;r respons. ICVA inledde sitt arbete 1962 (&#xf6;ver 50 &#xe5;r sedan). ICVAs verksamhetsomr&#xe5;den &#xe4;r 1. tv&#xe5;ngsf&#xf6;rflyttningar/flyktingfr&#xe5;gor, 2. humanit&#xe4;rt partnerskap och principer, 3. humanit&#xe4;r samordning och 4. humanit&#xe4;r finansiering med syfte att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra humanit&#xe4;rt partnersskap, praxis och policy. Detta g&#xf6;rs bl.a. genom deltagande i Interagency Standing Committee (IASC) m&#xf6;ten och arbetsgrupper samt genom regionalt och lokalt arbete bidra till l&#xe4;rande och kapacitetsutveckling hos dess medlemmar. 
 
ICVA har l&#xe4;mnat in en ans&#xf6;kan till Sida om 7 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d under en 27 m&#xe5;naders period f&#xf6;r att bidra till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra den humanit&#xe4;ra samordning och st&#xe4;rka humanit&#xe4;ra systemets effektivitet genom mer systematiskt, konsekvent och proaktivt CSO engagemang. Den planerade aktivitetsperioden l&#xf6;per fr&#xe5;n 1 oktober 2015 till 31 december 2017.

Sida kan genom st&#xf6;d till ICVA bidra till att strategiskt p&#xe5;verka det humanit&#xe4;ra systemet genom IASC och global, regionala och lokala CSOer som arbetar med humanit&#xe4;ra fr&#xe5;gor.

ICVA &#xe4;r stratgiskt mycket viktigt inf&#xf6;r World Humanitarian Summit 2016 f&#xf6;r att f&#xe5; in det lokala, nationella perspektivet.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICVA&apos;s overarching objective is to leverage the advantages of all entities involved in humanitarian action, including regional organizations, national NGOs and international NGOs, to promote principled and effective humanitarian action. To this end, ICVA focuses on four programmatic areas covering: forced displacement; humanitarian partnerships and principles; humanitarian coordination, and; humanitarian financing.
In 2017, ICVA&apos;s work was predominantly oriented around influencing the outcomes of processes launched in 2016, namely: the Grand Bargain on humanitarian financing; the New York Declaration proposing Global Compacts on Refugees and Migrants, and; the &quot;New way of Working&quot;.
ICVA aims to support its members and other NGOs to make sense of and follow these global processes by producing a series of briefing papers on each work process, with further information shared and disseminated through webinars.
For 2016-2017 the strategic intent is to promote NGO engagement in the development of the humanitarian sector and policies, for more collective, principled and effective action - with a special focus in forced displacement, humanitarian partnership and principles, humanitarian coordination and humanitarian financing.   2013-2015: ICVA&#x2019;s strategic intent is to support NGOs&apos; knowledge sharing, dialogue and collective advocacy for strengthened humanitarian partnerships, practices and policies.</narrative>
  </description>
